krauken (0.1.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Internal architecture: the daemon composition root no longer
    constructs or knows about any concrete hardware platform class
    (BrewPiConnection, TiltScanner, ManualIpcConnection,
    SimulatorIpcConnection) or their configuration (socket paths,
    KRAUKEN_TILT_HCI_DEVICE) -- platforms/registry.py's new
    PlatformRegistry class now owns constructing and running all of
    them, via each platform's own build_state factory. No user-facing
    behavior change; verified locally end-to-end with Playwright
    (hardware discovery, role mapping, live control-tick dispatch) and
    on a real running instance before release.
  * KRAUKEN_SIMULATOR_TILT_ENABLED (default on, since Krauken isn't in
    production yet) gates the Simulator's second ("Simulated Tilt")
    discover() candidate independently of its chamber candidate.

 -- The Krauken Project <dneumann@arpio.io>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 15:35:03 -0400

krauken (0.1.2) stable; urgency=high

  * Fix: krauken-api.service specified User=krauken-api -- a user that
    never actually gets created anywhere (postinst only ever provisions
    the single shared "krauken" system user, matching every other unit).
    Caught via a real install: systemd exit code 217 (EXIT_USER) and an
    endless activating/auto-restart crash loop. Now User=krauken,
    matching krauken-daemon/-manual/-simulator/-supervisor.
  * Fix: all five .service units had StartLimitIntervalSec/
    StartLimitBurst in [Service], where systemd silently ignores them
    ("Unknown key ... in section [Service]", visible in `journalctl`/
    `systemctl status` on a real install) -- these are [Unit]-level
    directives. Moved accordingly; the crash-loop rate limit was never
    actually being enforced until this fix.

 -- The Krauken Project <dneumann@arpio.io>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:37:38 -0400

krauken (0.1.1) stable; urgency=high

  * Fix: dh_installsystemd's default lookup only ever matches a single
    debian/<package>.<EXTENSION> unit named after the package itself --
    it does not glob debian/<package>.<name>.service for multiple,
    differently-named units on its own. v0.1.0 shipped with zero
    systemd units installed as a result (confirmed via a real install:
    dpkg -L krauken listed no unit files, systemctl couldn't find
    krauken-api/krauken-daemon, the API was never running). Added an
    explicit override_dh_installsystemd in debian/rules naming each of
    the four real units (krauken-supervisor deliberately excluded --
    not yet functional, see its own unit file comment).
  * Fix: krauken.postinst's own introductory comment spelled out the
    literal #DEBHELPER# token while describing it, which
    dh_installdeb's plain text substitution then spliced the real
    generated snippet into -- left a stray word behind that the shell
    printed "not found" for. Harmless in practice (landed before `set
    -e` took effect) but alarming; reworded to not repeat the literal
    token.

